# Railway staging environment variables

Copy into the **staging** app service Variables tab.
Use a separate Postgres service in the staging environment (never point staging at prod DB).

```text
DATABASE_URL=${{Postgres.DATABASE_URL}}
```

(Adjust `Postgres` to the staging database service name if different.)

BASE_URL=https://beacon-staging.magiconair.net
SECURE_COOKIES=true
WEBAUTHN_RP_ID=beacon-staging.magiconair.net
WEBAUTHN_RP_DISPLAY_NAME=Beacon Staging
WEBAUTHN_RP_ORIGINS=https://beacon-staging.magiconair.net

BOOTSTRAP_ADMIN_EMAIL=rhc@example.com
BOOTSTRAP_REISSUE=false

# Required by the current binary until identity sealing is removed.
IDENTITY_PUBLIC_KEY_B64=
IDENTITY_KEY_ID=staging-1

# Until custom DNS exists, use Railway's generated HTTPS URL instead:
# BASE_URL=https://<your-staging-service>.up.railway.app
# WEBAUTHN_RP_ID=<your-staging-service>.up.railway.app
# WEBAUTHN_RP_ORIGINS=https://<your-staging-service>.up.railway.app
